One Durable Object instance per board gives you a single source of truth, and the **WebSocket Hibernation API** lets Cloudflare evict the DO from memory while keeping sockets open — so an idle board costs nothing until a message arrives.

**Structure:**
- `Worker` — routes `/board/:id/ws` requests, upgrades to WebSocket, forwards to the right DO via `idFromName(boardId)`.
- `BoardDO` (Durable Object, SQLite-backed) — owns the board state, accepts hibernatable WebSockets, persists edits, and fans out to all connected sockets.

```ts
// worker.ts
export interface Env {
  BOARD: DurableObjectNamespace<BoardDO>;
}

export default {
  async fetch(req: Request, env: Env) {
    const url = new URL(req.url);
    const boardId = url.pathname.split("/")[2];
    const stub = env.BOARD.getByName(boardId);
    return stub.fetch(req); // upgrade happens inside the DO
  },
};
```

```ts
// board-do.ts
import { DurableObject } from "cloudflare:workers";

export class BoardDO extends DurableObject<Env> {
  constructor(ctx: DurableObjectState, env: Env) {
    super(ctx, env);
    ctx.blockConcurrencyWhile(async () => {
      this.ctx.storage.sql.exec(`
        CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS strokes (
          id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
          data TEXT NOT NULL
        )`);
    });
  }

  async fetch(req: Request) {
    const { 0: client, 1: server } = new WebSocketPair();
    // Hibernation: DO can be evicted from memory; socket stays open
    this.ctx.acceptWebSocket(server);
    return new Response(null, { status: 101, webSocket: client });
  }

  async webSocketMessage(ws: WebSocket, message: string) {
    this.ctx.storage.sql.exec(
      "INSERT INTO strokes (data) VALUES (?)",
      message
    );
    for (const peer of this.ctx.getWebSockets()) {
      if (peer !== ws) peer.send(message);
    }
  }

  async webSocketClose(ws: WebSocket) {
    ws.close();
  }
}
```

Key points:
- `ctx.acceptWebSocket()` (not a plain `.accept()`) enables hibernation — connections survive DO eviction, and you're only billed for active CPU time, not idle wall-clock time.
- `ctx.getWebSockets()` retrieves live sockets after wake-up, so you don't need to keep an in-memory connection list.
- Persist each stroke to SQLite storage synchronously before fan-out, so a reconnecting client (or a freshly-woken DO) can replay board state from `SELECT * FROM strokes`.
- `getByName(boardId)` gives deterministic routing — same board ID always hits the same DO instance, which is your single source of truth.

