## Durable Object (state + fan-out)

```ts
import { DurableObject } from "cloudflare:workers";

export class Board extends DurableObject<Env> {
  constructor(ctx: DurableObjectState, env: Env) {
    super(ctx, env);
    ctx.blockConcurrencyWhile(async () => {
      this.ctx.storage.sql.exec(`
        CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS ops (
          id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,
          data TEXT NOT NULL
        )`);
    });
  }

  async fetch(req: Request) {
    const pair = new WebSocketPair();
    const [client, server] = Object.values(pair);
    this.ctx.acceptWebSocket(server); // hibernatable — no in-memory listener cost while idle
    return new Response(null, { status: 101, webSocket: client });
  }

  // Called on wake, even after hibernation evicted the DO
  async webSocketMessage(ws: WebSocket, message: string) {
    this.ctx.storage.sql.exec("INSERT INTO ops (data) VALUES (?)", message);
    for (const peer of this.ctx.getWebSockets()) {
      if (peer !== ws) peer.send(message); // fan-out
    }
  }

  async webSocketClose(ws: WebSocket, code: number) {
    ws.close(code, "board closing");
  }
}
```

## Why this satisfies "idle costs nothing"

- `ctx.acceptWebSocket` + returning from `fetch()` lets the DO **hibernate** — it's evicted from memory and stops billing for duration while sockets stay open; `webSocketMessage`/`webSocketClose` wake it on demand.
- Per-board DOs mean idle boards have zero active compute and only pay for storage reads/writes on actual edits — no polling, no global always-on process.
- On wake, reconstruct any needed in-memory cache (e.g., cursor positions) from `ctx.getWebSockets()` tags and SQLite rather than keeping it live.

